65,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000070718","module":"turquoise","kme":0.276969,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.446504,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000070718","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0895861,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.704234,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000070718","entrez_id":["10947"],"uniprot":["P53677"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a subunit of the heterotetrameric adaptor-related protein comlex 3 (AP-3), which belongs to the adaptor complexes medium subunits family. The AP-3 complex plays a role in protein trafficking to lysosomes and specialized organelles. Multiple alternatively spliced variants, encoding the same protein, have been identified. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P53677","text":"Part of the AP-3 complex, an adaptor-related complex which is not clathrin-associated. The complex is associated with the Golgi region as well as more peripheral structures. It facilitates the budding of vesicles from the Golgi membrane and may be directly involved in trafficking to lysosomes. In concert with the BLOC-1 complex, AP-3 is required to target cargos into vesicles assembled at cell bodies for delivery into neurites and nerve terminals."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}